Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts it as a message via the Slack API to the specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXXX/YYYYY/ZZZZZ'; // Replace with your Slack webhook URL
  const payload = {
    "text": text,
    "channel": channel
  };

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  })
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => console.log('Message posted to Slack:', data))
  .catch(error => console.error('Error posting to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello from JavaScript!', '#general');
```

Replace `'https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXXX/YYYYY/ZZZZZ'` with your actual Slack webhook URL. You can find your webhook URL by going to your Slack workspace settings, clicking on "Incoming Webhooks", and then copying the URL for the channel you want to use.

